OL,3,GNEWSACouncil facing #8.7m overspend,
OL,4,Areport says
OL,5,
OL,6,FHowever, the council's executive member
OL,7,Ffor finance Nicky Walker said work was
OL,8,Fbeing undertaken to reduce expenditure.
OL,9,FThe authority said last financial year
OL,10,Fended with a #1.8m overspend, a much
OL,11,Freduced figure on what was forecast at
OL,12,Fthis time in 2025.
OL,14,FWalker said the most significant
OL,15,Fpressures were in children's care due
OL,16,Fto agency staffing, an increased number
OL,17,Fof children being looked after and
OL,18,Femergency resource workers.
